1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,277
We're SARcastic Scientists from Islamabad:

2
00:00:03,317 --> 00:00:06,940
Saeed Ahmad, Shaharyar Sajid and Usama Hussain.

3
00:00:06,980 --> 00:00:08,460
This is SARtale.

4
00:00:08,850 --> 00:00:13,298
In 2022, a glacial lake above Hunza burst and swept away the

5
00:00:13,338 --> 00:00:15,406
Karakoram Highway bridge.

6
00:00:15,446 --> 00:00:19,350
Pakistan has more than three thousand glacial lakes.

7
00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:23,081
They fill in summer, exactly when cloud hides them.

8
00:00:23,121 --> 00:00:26,819
This July, Pakistan's space agency said cloud limited its

9
00:00:26,859 --> 00:00:27,590
checks.

10
00:00:27,980 --> 00:00:32,839
NISAR, the new radar from NASA and ISRO, sees through cloud.

11
00:00:32,879 --> 00:00:36,179
At Attabad, the optical image is cloud;

12
00:00:36,219 --> 00:00:38,480
the radar shows the lake.

13
00:00:38,870 --> 00:00:40,319
We built SARtale.

14
00:00:40,359 --> 00:00:44,397
It reads every pass over thirty-nine lakes, measures each

15
00:00:44,437 --> 00:00:48,410
lake's water against its own normal range, and gives one

16
00:00:48,450 --> 00:00:51,970
plain status, with what to do and who to contact.

17
00:00:52,360 --> 00:00:56,080
It refreshes every week, and anyone can request a new lake.
